    {
      "title": "Brazil runoff live updates: Flávio Bolsonaro calls for election results to be ‘annulled’ after historic loss to Lula",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula",
      "description": "<p>Leftist president Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva defeated the far-right senator and was elected president of Brazil for a fourth non-consecutive term</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/lula-wins-brazil-election\">Full report: Lula wins fourth term as Brazil’s president over Flávio Bolsonaro</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-2026-live-second-round-results\">Live second round results</a></p></li></ul><p>The local electoral court ordered the immediate restoration of 100% of the bus fleet and ordered the arrest of the municipal transport secretary, Pablo Souza, on suspicion of an electoral offence and disobeying court orders. The arrest warrant could not be carried out, however, because he is in Paris on what the city government described as an “official mission”, and is not expected to return to Brazil until Monday.</p><p>Late in the afternoon, Flávio Bolsonaro also filed requests for voting to be extended by two hours in cities in the states of São Paulo, Paraná and Santa Catarina, but because of heavy rain that he said had prevented voters from turning out.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-26T01:59:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lula wins fourth term as Brazil president after historic upset over far-right Flávio Bolsonaro",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/lula-wins-brazil-election",
      "description": "<p>Leftist incumbent Lula stages unprecedented comeback weeks after narrowly losing first round of election to Bolsonaro</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula\">Lula wins election in stunning comeback – live updates</a></p></li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva\">Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva</a>, the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva\">Brazilian</a> president, has staged a dramatic <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/27/viscerally-dedicated-to-social-issues-behind-lulas-drive-to-win-final-term-in-brazils-crunch-election\">election fightback</a>, defeating his far-right opponent, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/fl-vio-bolsonaro\">Flávio Bolsonaro</a>, to claim a historic fourth term in power.</p><p>With nearly 99% of votes counted the 80-year-old leftist received 51.75% of the vote to his 45-year-old rival’s 48.25%.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/lula-wins-brazil-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-26T00:19:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "Brazil election 2026: Full second round results as Lula wins comeback against Flávio Bolsonaro",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-2026-live-second-round-results",
      "description": "<p>After a shock defeat in the first round, the incumbent Brazilian president, Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva,<strong> </strong>has turned the election around to win the runoff.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula\">Live blog: latest analysis and reaction</a></p><p>Brazil’s president is elected purely by the popular vote. A winning candidate needs one more vote than 50% of votes cast; there is no role for the parliament and no electoral college.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-2026-live-second-round-results\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-26T00:15:36"
    },
